  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme/yeso",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca formada por el mineral del mismo nombre, de fórmula caso4.2h2o, perteneciente a la clase de los sulfatos, que cristaliza en el sistema monoclínico y se presenta con aspecto fibroso, en cristales de gran tamaño o en maclas, entre ellas las de punta de flecha. tiene dureza 2 en la escala de mohs, rayándose con la uña. es incoloro o presenta color blanco, gris, amarillo o rojo, tiene brillo vítreo o nacarado y varía de transparente a translúcido"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Rock formed by the mineral of the same name, with the formula CaSO4·2H2O, belonging to the class of sulfates, crystallizing in the monoclinic system and occurring in fibrous form, as large crystals or as twins, including arrowhead twins. It has a hardness of 2 on the Mohs scale, being scratched by a fingernail. It is colourless or white, grey, yellow or red, with vitreous or pearly lustre and varying from transparent to translucent"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/LithologyValue/gypsumOrAnhydrite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/rock_gypsum_or_anhydrite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "yeso"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "gypsum"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/material-igme"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
